CHANGES:
* update from 2.3 to 6.5.5
* switch to Python 3 (MODPY_VERSION = ${MODPY_DEFAULT_VERSION_3})
* use MODPY_PYBUILD = setuptools, drop MODPY_SETUPTOOLS
* refresh WANTLIB for the new GTK3/GTK3-based build
* add LIB_DEPENDS on x11/gnome/at-spi2-core and devel/gettext
  (fixes broken devel/at-spi2-core and devel/gettext-runtime paths)
* build without Xdummy, uinput, pam, service, sd_listen, wayland
  client/server, v4l2 and wireshark
* install configuration under share/examples/xpra
* replace patch-setup_py and patch-xpra_buffers_memalign_c with
  patch-setup_py_cups and patch-setup_py_keyboard
* regenerate PLIST

TESTING:
Builds, packages and runs on OpenBSD 8.0/amd64.  "xpra start :99"
reports "xpra seamless server version 6.5.5-r0" and "xpra info :99"
returns session information.  "make update-plist" is idempotent and
"make lib-depends-check" is clean.

